{"kind":"event","event_id":5009,"event_uid":"01M2KQV0C6FC54YV7T2KDFJX84","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":226,"issue_uid":"01M2KP4Y0ZKARPDX4AZ0N175D8","issue_short_id":"75d8","actor":"impl:1@run-14","hlc_physical_ms":1789516415366,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"8555a2dada338489e9fc4cd295234a0370a45b1b468f28a9082051e11ce5413b","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2KQV0C5EFKZXC6BPDV7FAZP","author":"impl:1@run-14","body":"task 1 (trash table) starting at f24d405. Approach as the Context dictates: one shared todo-cells literal reused for `todos` and `trash` in TABLES_SCHEMA; `deleteTodo` becomes a single transaction (hasRow guard, delTable('trash'), setRow('trash', id, getRow('todos', id)), delRow('todos', id)); new `undoDelete(store)` a single transaction looping getRowIds('trash'); a second INVARIANTS entry for 'trash' that is the todos rule applied to a trashed row. Then the three new expected JSON files, and the loosening of the BASE pins (smoke, done-count leg (o), todos-store leg (c), and the four linter test files off exact counts/lists onto lower bounds and toContain). Not writing tests/state-exams/delete-to-trash.test.ts — a peer's exam lands there.","created_at":"2026-09-15T23:53:35.365134093Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T23:53:35.366Z"}
